│ Okay, let’s address this persistent issue. The core problem is     │
│ that the __str__ method of MyObject is returning the enum value    │
│ directly, which isn't the string representation intended. We need  │
│ to ensure it returns the string value associated with the          │
│ my_str_value field.                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ Reasoning:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The MyChoice enum provides string representations for its choices. │
│ The MyObject model’s my_str_value field stores these string        │
│ values. The __str__ method of MyObject should therefore return the │
│ string value associated with the field, not the enum value itself. │
│ This will ensure that when the object is converted to a string     │
│ (e.g., when logging or displaying it), the correct string          │
│ representation is used.                                            │
